{"page": 3, "segments": [{"index": 0, "text": "Dimension\nInsertion Sort\nMerge Sort", "rects": [[64.5, 56.994232177734375, 129.30001831054688, 70.5902328491211], [159.40672302246094, 56.994232177734375, 260.206787109375, 70.5902328491211], [380.7622985839844, 56.994232177734375, 452.7621765136719, 70.5902328491211]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/5ecc50eb/pages/3/audio/seg_0000.wav", "duration": 4.9}, {"index": 1, "text": "Crossover\nAlways exists a point where\nmerge sort wins\n\u2014", "rects": [[64.5, 80.38485717773438, 129.30001831054688, 93.9808578491211], [159.40672302246094, 73.58798217773438, 353.8068542480469, 87.1839828491211], [159.40672302246094, 87.18173217773438, 267.40679931640625, 100.7777328491211], [380.7622985839844, 80.38485717773438, 387.9623107910156, 93.9808578491211]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/5ecc50eb/pages/3/audio/seg_0001.wav", "duration": 5.9}, {"index": 2, "text": "Computer A (10 billion instr/sec, insertion sort, 2n\u00b2\ninstructions) vs Computer B (10 million instr/sec, merge\nsort, 50n\u00b7lg n instructions): For 10M numbers, Computer B\nruns >17\u00d7 faster than Computer A despite being 1000\u00d7 slower\nin raw power.", "rects": [[92.25, 115.02548217773438, 473.8499755859375, 128.62149047851562], [92.25, 128.61923217773438, 495.4499206542969, 142.21524047851562], [92.25, 142.21298217773438, 502.64990234375, 155.80899047851562], [92.25, 155.80673217773438, 517.0498657226562, 169.40274047851562], [92.25, 169.40048217773438, 185.8500518798828, 182.99649047851562]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/5ecc50eb/pages/3/audio/seg_0002.wav", "duration": 22.925}, {"index": 3, "text": "For 100M numbers, insertion sort takes >23\ndays, merge sort <4 hours.", "rects": [[193.05006408691406, 169.40048217773438, 495.4499206542969, 182.99649047851562], [92.25, 182.99423217773438, 279.45013427734375, 196.59024047851562]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/5ecc50eb/pages/3/audio/seg_0003.wav", "duration": 6.325}, {"index": 4, "text": "Formulas & Equations", "rects": [[62.25, 212.5479736328125, 206.25006103515625, 226.14398193359375]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/5ecc50eb/pages/3/audio/seg_0004.wav", "duration": 2.075}, {"index": 5, "text": "Efficiency comparison formula", "rects": [[62.25, 242.77621459960938, 235.54483032226562, 254.06028747558594]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/5ecc50eb/pages/3/audio/seg_0005.wav", "duration": 2.5}, {"index": 6, "text": "(Computer A time for n=10M) = (2\u00b7(10\u21d4)\u00b2 instructions) / (10\u00b9\u21d4 \ninstr/sec) = 20,000 sec \u2248 5.56 hours (Computer B time for n=10M) \n= (50\u00b710\u21d4\u00b7lg(10\u21d4) instructions) / (10\u21d4 instr/sec) \u2248 1,163 sec \u2248 \n19.4 min", "rects": [[62.25, 270.6903381347656, 509.2498779296875, 284.2863464355469], [62.25, 284.2840881347656, 530.2930297851562, 297.8800964355469], [62.25, 297.8778381347656, 523.9498291015625, 311.4738464355469], [62.25, 311.4715881347656, 119.85000610351562, 325.0675964355469]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/5ecc50eb/pages/3/audio/seg_0006.wav", "duration": 26.325}, {"index": 7, "text": "Rules, Laws & Theorems", "rects": [[62.25, 341.0253601074219, 220.6500701904297, 354.6213684082031]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/5ecc50eb/pages/3/audio/seg_0007.wav", "duration": 2.3}, {"index": 8, "text": "Property of NP-complete problems", "rects": [[62.25, 371.25360107421875, 253.47189331054688, 382.5376892089844]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/5ecc50eb/pages/3/audio/seg_0008.wav", "duration": 2.65}, {"index": 9, "text": "Statement: If an efficient algorithm exists for any one NP-\ncomplete problem, then efficient algorithms exist for all of\nthem.\nSignificance: A small change to the problem statement can\ncause a big change to the efficiency of the best known\nalgorithm.", "rects": [[92.25, 399.167724609375, 517.0603637695312, 412.76373291015625], [92.25, 412.761474609375, 524.2498168945312, 426.35748291015625], [92.25, 426.355224609375, 128.25001525878906, 439.95123291015625], [92.25, 439.948974609375, 502.6639099121094, 453.54498291015625], [92.25, 453.542724609375, 481.0499572753906, 467.13873291015625], [92.25, 467.136474609375, 164.2500457763672, 480.73248291015625]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/5ecc50eb/pages/3/audio/seg_0009.wav", "duration": 18.575}, {"index": 10, "text": "Reason to study algorithms even with infinite/free resources", "rects": [[62.25, 497.3647155761719, 420.7912902832031, 508.6488037109375]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/5ecc50eb/pages/3/audio/seg_0010.wav", "duration": 4.375}, {"index": 11, "text": "Statement: You would still like to be certain that your\nsolution method terminates and does so with the correct\nanswer.", "rects": [[92.25, 525.2789306640625, 488.2604675292969, 538.8748779296875], [92.25, 538.8726806640625, 488.24993896484375, 552.4686279296875], [92.25, 552.4664306640625, 142.6500244140625, 566.0623779296875]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/5ecc50eb/pages/3/audio/seg_0011.wav", "duration": 8.125}, {"index": 12, "text": "Algorithm as a technology", "rects": [[62.25, 582.694580078125, 211.64205932617188, 593.9786987304688]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/5ecc50eb/pages/3/audio/seg_0012.wav", "duration": 2.375}, {"index": 13, "text": "Statement: Total system performance depends on choosing\nefficient algorithms as much as on choosing fast hardware.", "rects": [[92.25, 610.6087646484375, 488.2604675292969, 624.2047119140625], [92.25, 624.2025146484375, 509.8498840332031, 637.7984619140625]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/5ecc50eb/pages/3/audio/seg_0013.wav", "duration": 7.875}, {"index": 14, "text": "Edge Cases & Pitfalls", "rects": [[62.25, 653.7562866210938, 213.45005798339844, 667.3522338867188]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/5ecc50eb/pages/3/audio/seg_0014.wav", "duration": 2.075}, {"index": 15, "text": "\u201cIncorrect algorithms can sometimes be useful, if you can\ncontrol their error rate\u201d \u2014 e.g., algorithms for finding\nlarge prime numbers with controllable error rate (Ch. 31).\nNo efficient algorithm known for NP-complete problems, but\nnobody has ever proven one cannot exist.", "rects": [[92.25, 683.3099975585938, 502.64990234375, 696.9059448242188], [92.25, 696.9037475585938, 495.4499206542969, 710.4996948242188], [92.25, 710.4974975585938, 509.8498840332031, 724.0934448242188], [92.25, 724.0912475585938, 509.8498840332031, 737.6871948242188], [92.25, 737.6849975585938, 380.25018310546875, 751.2809448242188]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/5ecc50eb/pages/3/audio/seg_0015.wav", "duration": 20.525}, {"index": 16, "text": "\u2022", "rects": [[77.84765625, 115.02548217773438, 85.04765319824219, 128.62149047851562], [77.84765625, 399.167724609375, 85.04765319824219, 412.76373291015625], [77.84765625, 439.948974609375, 85.04765319824219, 453.54498291015625], [77.84765625, 525.2789306640625, 85.04765319824219, 538.8748779296875], [77.84765625, 610.6087646484375, 85.04765319824219, 624.2047119140625], [77.84765625, 683.3099975585938, 85.04765319824219, 696.9059448242188], [77.84765625, 724.0912475585938, 85.04765319824219, 737.6871948242188]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/5ecc50eb/pages/3/audio/seg_0016.wav", "duration": 0}, {"index": 17, "text": "\u2022", "rects": [[77.84765625, 115.02548217773438, 85.04765319824219, 128.62149047851562], [77.84765625, 399.167724609375, 85.04765319824219, 412.76373291015625], [77.84765625, 439.948974609375, 85.04765319824219, 453.54498291015625], [77.84765625, 525.2789306640625, 85.04765319824219, 538.8748779296875], [77.84765625, 610.6087646484375, 85.04765319824219, 624.2047119140625], [77.84765625, 683.3099975585938, 85.04765319824219, 696.9059448242188], [77.84765625, 724.0912475585938, 85.04765319824219, 737.6871948242188]], "audio_url": "/static/sessions/5ecc50eb/pages/3/audio/seg_0017.wav", "duration": 0}, {"index": 18, "text": "\u2022", "rects": [[77.84765625, 115.02548217773438, 85.04765319824219, 128.62149047851562], [77.84765625, 399.167724609375, 85.04765319824219, 412.76373291015625], [77.84765625, 439.